WHAT: `pollOnce` reads a single page and then advances the cursor to `pollStartedAt`, but `PAGE_SIZE = 500` does not make that page exhaustive — the EventsClient contract (events-client.ts:16-17) says the provider caps `limit` at 100 and still returns at most 100 events, so `page.hasMore` becomes true whenever >100 events exist in the window. WHY: The remaining events are never fetched and the cursor still jumps past them, so their invoices are never marked paid/voided/past-due — silent, permanent billing-state loss (the comment on lines 15-16 asserting hasMore is never true is false). HOW: loop until `hasMore` is false, passing `nextCursor` as `cursor`, before setting the cursor:
```ts
let cursor: string | undefined;
let page;
do {
  page = await client.listEvents({ createdAfter: since, createdBefore: pollStartedAt, limit: PAGE_SIZE, cursor });
  for (const event of page.data) await handleEvent(invoices, event);
  cursor = page.nextCursor ?? undefined;
} while (page.hasMore);
await cursors.set(CURSOR_KEY, pollStartedAt);
```

